# Zero Fitness Compose Conventions

For mockup-driven UI work, follow the repo skills `design-to-compose-01-build`, `design-to-compose-02-review`, and `design-to-compose-03-verify`. This rule adds **project-specific** paths and patterns; the skills stay generic.

## Design references

- Mockups: `docs/design/mockups/`. Match the requested screen by HTML comments, labels, and visible copy; treat HTML/CSS as design intent, not implementation.

## Theme and shared UI

- Palette and scheme: `app/src/main/java/com/zero/fitness/ui/theme/` (`Color.kt`, `Theme.kt`). Extend these before adding new colors in components.
- Reuse `MaterialTheme` roles and existing tokens. Wrap previews in `ZeroFitnessTheme`; prefer `dynamicColor = false` in previews for stable comparison with mockups.
- Shared components: `app/src/main/java/com/zero/fitness/ui/screens/common/` — prefer `AppBar`, `AppButton`, `Bubble`, `InteractiveBubble`, `AppToggle`, and related APIs when semantics fit.

## Defaults pattern (required for new shared components)

Mirror `AppButtonDefaults`, `BubblesDefaults`, `AppBarDefaults`, and `AppToggleDefaults`:

- `<Component>Defaults` with `@Immutable` token data classes and `@Composable` factories defaulting to `ui/theme` (not inline hex in composable bodies).
- Public composables accept optional `colors` / `sizes` (or equivalent) defaulting to those factories.

## Strings

- User-facing and accessibility copy: `app/src/main/res/values/strings.xml`. Mirror and translate every new key in every existing locale file (`values-sr/strings.xml` today). See `.cursor/rules/zero-fitness-strings.mdc`.
- Load with `stringResource(R.string.*)` — not hardcoded production strings.
- Generic shared composables take `String` parameters where needed; feature-specific layouts and copy belong under the feature package (for example `TrackWeightToggleSettingCard` in `ui/screens/workout/exercise/`).
- Previews use the same `stringResource` keys as production. Do not use preview-only literals or stale-`R` workarounds; rebuild the app module if generated `R` is out of date.

## Screens and architecture

- Feature UI under `ui/screens/<feature>/`. Reusable UI stays stateless with callbacks; connect to the feature ViewModel (or existing state holder) at the screen boundary.
- Navigation: typed Navigation Compose (`@Serializable`, `NavGraphBuilder` extensions, `NavController` helpers) as elsewhere in the project.

## Layout and accessibility

- Material 3 and existing dependencies only; no new libraries solely to mimic mockup details.
- `FlowRow` for wrapping chips/options; lazy containers for long or repeating lists.
- Meaningful semantics, adequate touch targets, scrollable forms on small screens.

## Verification

- IDE diagnostics on edited Kotlin files.
- Gradle: `./gradlew :app:compileDebugKotlin` (or full rebuild if resources changed).
